摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Remotely control DeepSeek Harness from your phone: Android App + cloud relay + PC plugin. One persistent QR code, three uses — download, pairing, and login/grant.","id":"gh:1335797219","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dshmobile","slug":"zdx8637-gitdog/dshmobile","topics":["android","deepseek-harness","deepseek-harness-plugin","deepseek-harness-plugins","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins","remote-control"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Remotely control DeepSeek Harness from your phone: Android App + cloud relay + PC plugin. One persis"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"tent QR code, three uses — download, pairing, and login/grant."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dshmobile — Remote Mobile Client for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"中文文档"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**Zero-friction**: install the plugin once → scan a QR code → keep working from your phone.\nA true R"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"emote Client for DSH — no Tailscale, tunnels, port forwarding, NAT, or networking knowledge\nrequired"},{"id":"p4s3","text":", no DSH modifications, cross-platform."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Control your local DeepSeek Harness (DSH) from your phone: scan to pair → device → session tree →\nch"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"at, approvals, question answering, model switching, file browsing."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Business content (prompts / replies / sessions / files) is protected by **E2EE end-to-end\nencryption"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"**: the relay only sees routing metadata — it can neither read nor tamper with your\nsession content."},{"id":"p8s3","text":" The connection layer self-heals: after a DSH restart or a network hiccup it\nre-handshakes automatic"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"ally, no manual steps required."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Open Source & Security"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| Component | Status | Notes |\n| :-- | :-- | :-- |\n| **PC Bridge / plugin** | Open Source (MIT) | `p"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"lugins/`, npm package `@zdx8637/dshmobile-bridge` |\n| **Protocol contract** | Open | `docs/02-protoc"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"ol.md` (single source of truth for the wire format) |\n| **E2EE design** | Open and auditable | `docs"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"/plan-e2ee.md` (threat model + crypto parameters + handshake) |\n| **Android App** | Signed APK distr"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"ibution | Download by scanning the QR code |\n| **Cloud Relay** | Hosted service | Auth / routing / a"},{"id":"p10s6","text":"n | Download by scanning the QR code |\n| **Cloud Relay** | Hosted service | Auth / routing / audit |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The protocol and crypto implementations are fully public and independently auditable; business\nconte"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"nt is end-to-end encrypted, and the relay only forwards routing metadata — it cannot read\nyour sessi"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"s end-to-end encrypted, and the relay only forwards routing metadata — it cannot read\nyour sessions."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"**Pick your path first**: DSH **desktop app 0.2.0 or newer** → §A (GUI, recommended); legacy\n`dsh we"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"b` (**0.1.7**) → §B (CLI). Both install the same package\n`@zdx8637/dshmobile-bridge` (current plugin"},{"id":"p13s3","text":" version **1.0.7**)."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### A. PC — DSH 0.2.0 desktop app: install from the GUI (recommended)"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"1. Open the DSH desktop app → plugin manager → click **「添加插件」** (Add plugin);\n2. Paste the package n"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ame **with an exact version** into the input box (its placeholder reads\n「输入插件的包名、GitHub 仓库地址或本地目录路径。"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"」 — a GitHub repository URL or a local directory\npath is accepted there too):"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"3. On the right pick **「安装源」** — `npm 官方源` (official npm registry) or `中国大陆镜像源`\n(Mainland-China mirr"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"or) — whichever your network reaches;\n4. Click install;\n5. **Restart DSH** — the host has to reload "},{"id":"p17s3","text":"the plugin before it takes effect;\n6. Open the panel: a ▶ arrow appears at the bottom of the web sid"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"ebar — click to open it\n(① login / grant code, ② encrypted pairing code)."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"> ⚠️ **Always pin an exact version** (e.g. `@zdx8637/dshmobile-bridge@1.0.7`). The profile directory"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"\n> contains a `pnpm-lock.yaml`; when you reinstall by bare package name the lockfile can pin the\n> v"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"ersion back to the old one (measured: npm already served 1.0.2, yet a reinstall still left 1.0.0\n> i"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"k to the old one (measured: npm already served 1.0.2, yet a reinstall still left 1.0.0\n> installed)."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"> ⚠️ **Plugins do not auto-update.** The dialog says so outright —\n> 「插件安装后，暂不支持自动更新。若需升级，请先卸载再安装新版」"},{"id":"p19s2","text":". So to upgrade: uninstall in the\n> plugin manager first, then repeat the steps above with the new v"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"e: uninstall in the\n> plugin manager first, then repeat the steps above with the new version number."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### B. PC — DSH 0.1.7 (legacy: `dsh web` + CLI): install from the CLI"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"> Requires `pnpm` (the `dsh plugin` subcommand depends on it; `corepack enable` or\n> `npm i -g pnpm`"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"). Legacy only: npm `latest` for `@deepseek-ai/dsh` points at the 0.1.7 CLI, so\n> this command pulls"},{"id":"p22s3","text":" the 0.1.7 `dsh plugin`. **On 0.2.0 or newer use §A (the GUI) instead** — the CLI\n> is not the 0.2.0"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"h plugin`. **On 0.2.0 or newer use §A (the GUI) instead** — the CLI\n> is not the 0.2.0 install path."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"### Phone (Android App)"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Scan the QR code on the PC panel → download the signed APK from the landing page (current version\n**"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"v1.0.0**). Then scan in the App: ① first to log in, ② then for E2EE pairing — once paired, a\n**shiel"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"d badge** appears in the device list (E2EE is active). A shield with a slash means plaintext;\nboth a"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"re grey — the difference is the shape, not the colour."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## DSH Version Requirement"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"The plugin **supports the v2 protocol only, i.e. DSH v0.1.5 or newer**. The legacy protocol for\nolde"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"r DSH builds was **removed entirely** in `0.1.0-beta.23`."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| DSH version | Plugin behavior |\n| :-- | :-- |\n| **v0.1.5 or newer** | Full support: `/api` session"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" auth (launch token → session Cookie), Typert endpoints (`session/*` etc.), `/api/remote.mux` stream"},{"id":"p27s3","text":" multiplexing, `$events` approval/question waterfalls |\n| **v0.1.0-rc.6 or older** | **Not supported"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"** — upgrade DSH first, then install this plugin |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"> This is a deliberate narrowing: the dual-protocol branch was a long-standing defect hotspot, since"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"\n> every change had to be verified on both paths. If you are still on a pre-v2 DSH, stay on\n> `0.1.0"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"-beta.22`, or upgrade DSH first."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Directory"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"| Path | Contents |\n| :-- | :-- |\n| `plugins/` | PC Bridge plugin (host + bridge daemon + web panel)"},{"id":"p30s2","text":", open source |\n| `docs/02-protocol.md` | Relay envelopes, message types, device semantics (wire-for"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"mat contract) |\n| `docs/plan-e2ee.md` | E2EE v1 design (threat model, cryptography, handshake, pinni"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"ng) |\n| `docs/e2ee-identity-issues.md` | E2EE identity/pairing investigation (torn-read key regenera"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"tion, restart self-heal, etc.) |\n| `docs/bridge-singleton.md` | Bridge single-instance protection: w"},{"id":"p30s6","text":"hy duplicate bridges fight, the four defence layers, diagnostics |"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## Privacy & Secrets"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"This repository contains no real credentials. Android signing keys, relay account passwords, and\nser"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"ver SSH credentials live only in local/private channels — always injected via environment\nvariables "},{"id":"p32s3","text":"and referenced as placeholders in docs."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
